1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,990
A simple question at work
rarely has a simple source.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,570
The answer may be in Slack.

3
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,070
The task in Linear.

4
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,990
The implementation in GitHub.

5
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:09,370
The approval in Gmail.

6
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:11,415
QueueProof brings that
evidence together

7
00:00:11,415 --> 00:00:14,170
and lets you investigate it
as one connected system.

8
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,730
Ask a complex question,

9
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:18,090
and QueueProof retrieves
the relevant sources,

10
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:21,310
follows the people, issues,
commits, and timelines,

11
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:24,930
and builds an answer where every
important claim can be verified.

12
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:26,090
Now look at this.

13
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,030
GitHub proves the work shipped.

14
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:31,350
Linear independently shows
the same work is still open.

15
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:33,690
QueueProof does not guess
which system is right.

16
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:37,370
It preserves the contradiction,
shows both pieces of evidence,

17
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:41,350
reconstructs what happened, and
gives you the safest next action.

18
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:43,170
And it does not stop
at the dashboard.

19
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,915
Through MCP, the same
evidence layer works

20
00:00:45,915 --> 00:00:49,990
directly with Claude, ChatGPT,
and compatible AI agents.

21
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:52,610
So this is not another answer
generated from context.

22
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:56,275
It is an answer you can
inspect, trace, and defend.

23
00:00:56,275 --> 00:00:57,250
QueueProof.

24
00:00:57,340 --> 00:00:59,460
Ask your work. Get the proof.
